{"authorityRole":"external_auditor","by":"buger","candidateKey":"","candidateKind":"","changeKey":"pr/9056","createdAt":"2026-10-03T10:34:19Z","decision":"accept_change","decisionDigest":"sha256:7b53edc1f59d6c9a61df1b99689928534b35327602aa404b896c633f5aed476c","decisionId":"rdec-ecee806e1e345ea562067d9b194bbc86","identitySource":"github_login","packageDigest":"sha256:682c7203445d8324e8dd28110a6d546b73b507f24ba9dccaba55e7a1a0845aa6","packageIdentity":"epkg-fdffb6b61e5fd281e75b64e97fa396e25eb0c27b709adf08776f2204aea33686","prNumber":"9056","reason":"Recommend accepting: a new summon now answers the earlier waiting caller as cancelled instead of leaving it stuck (#9057), and the head b7bd59c4 also fixes the burst race found on the first commit. On a live Omarchy session, a burst of 20 summons left 19 callers stuck on quattro c05d9019, 7 to 12 on the first commit 0b4fe29, and 0 on b7bd59c4, in all 6 runs. The two-summon case exits cleanly, and a real selection still returns its value. A headless regression test for overlapping requests fails on both older trees and passes 8/8 on this head. One gap remains outside this PR: if the menu process dies after a summon, the caller still waits forever (tracked on #9057).","repo":"https://github.com/omacom/omarchy","schemaVersion":"reqproof.review-decision.v1","scope":"change"}
